e><publisher-name>World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>UNAIDS</collab></person-group><source>Overview of the Global AIDS Epidemic, 2006 Report on the Global AIDS Epidemic</source><year>2006</year><volume>Chapter 2</volume><publisher-name>UNAIDS</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Korea Immigration Bureau</collab></person-group><source>The Registered Foreigners According to Nationality and Eligibility in 2004</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Korea Immigration Bureau</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>HIV/AIDS in Asia and the Pacific Region 2003, HIV/AIDS status and trends in the Asia Pacific Region</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Korea Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab></person-group><source>The status of HIV/AIDS infection of Korea, Guidelines for HIV/AIDS Control</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>KCDC</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kee</surname><given-names>Mee-Kyung</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>Eun-Ju</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>Jin-Hee</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>Sung-Soon</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends in HIV seroprevalence in public health centers and blood bank(blood donations) in Republic of Korea; 2000&#x02013;2007</article-title><source>Infectious Diseases and Korean Society for Chemotherapy</source><year>2007</ye